      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will make trusty always run at LINUX_NICE_FOR_TRUSTY_PRIORITY_HIGH if trusty has not been updated which does not seem correct. You might be able to move the use_high_wq module_param into the file where you implemented trusty_get_requested_nice and take it into account there instead. As long as the path in sysfs does not change that might be simpler. On the other hand if use_high_wq changes from false to true, setting the priority of the threads only after trusty gets preempted might not be the best option. It might be better to have a helper function to set the priority based on multiple inputs (use_high_wq, pending nops and trusty priority requests).",
